# CODEOWNERS — requires review from the listed owners on changes to release-critical paths.
#
# This ONLY gates merges if "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in main's branch
# protection rule (Settings -> Branches -> main -> Require a pull request before merging ->
# Require review from Code Owners). Without that setting enabled, this file only suggests
# reviewers in the PR UI and enforces nothing — see docs/release-setup.md.
#
# Replace @coinspect/dappfence-admins with the actual maintainer team handle once created. A team
# is preferred over individual users so membership changes don't require editing this file.

# This file protects itself. Without this line, a single PR could both remove a restriction
# below and exploit it, needing only an ordinary (non-admin) reviewer.
.github/CODEOWNERS                @coinspect/dappfence-admins

# The release workflow itself: what the verify/publish jobs check and do, which key(s) it
# trusts (RELEASE_SIGNING_KEYS repo variable, admin-Settings-only to edit — see
# docs/release-setup.md), and which environment/permissions gate the actual npm publish.
.github/workflows/release.yml     @coinspect/dappfence-admins

# What gets published, and how versions are allowed to move.
packages/publish.json             @coinspect/dappfence-admins
scripts/sync-versions.js          @coinspect/dappfence-admins

# Describes the policy the paths above enforce; drift here is a documentation-trust problem,
# not just a typo.
docs/release-setup.md             @coinspect/dappfence-admins

# Lockfile: unreviewed changes here are a common way a supply-chain attack slips in.
package-lock.json                 @coinspect/dappfence-admins
